Coomi Life optional extension — psi-v2 cognitive engine

This directory contains a self-contained cognitive engine written for Coomi.
It uses only the Python standard library and makes no network requests.

Design informed by published research (concepts only, no code reused):
- Doerner's Psi theory: homeostatic needs driving cognition and emotion
- Russell's circumplex model of affect: valence x arousal emotion space
- Ebbinghaus forgetting curve and the testing effect: memory retention
- Gottman's research on relationship positivity ratios

An early prototype of this extension drew on community concepts from
LAAP AGI (https://github.com/ywbing-xrang/laap-AGI, Apache-2.0). The
current engine is an independent from-scratch implementation that shares
no code with that project and does not depend on it.

